It depends on what point in the game you are, and if you have access
to futher pet polymorphs. If you are lacking reflection, then you
probably should slay your silver dragon for that. See
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/DSM#Acquiring_dragon_scales for a
description how to do that safely.

If you want your pet to fight for you, the dragon is probably better,
but still way too slow for my taste. If you have magic resistance,
unchanging, or much patience, you can find a polytrap somewhere in the
Mines and polymorph further pets. I prefer vampire lords. They can
even clear out the castle if you give them a MC3 cloak, but won't last
through Gehennom.

If you want to wade though Gehennom, I'd take both along. Both will
eventually die. That's why I wouldn't put too much effort into kitting
out the salamander. The dragon will annoy you especially with his
constant eating. If you want manageable pets that can pack a punch
down there, a fully kitted out archon or the spell of charm monster
are usually the best solution. At least my pacifist games suggest so.
You can wish for the book or write it (1/3 chance with max Luck). As
for the archon, you can wish for a blessed figurine or go create
monster - charm monster farming in Vlad's tower.

Kitting out pets: see http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Pet#Equipment_for_pets
. In short, you want a fooproof +7 artifact weapon, magic resistance,
reflection, magic cancellation, good armor class, and a unicorn horn.


